+    "basic": "### What the screen shows\nEach part of the till has a row. The chips under it are the connections that can do that part, plus **Off** for the parts that are optional. A part marked *needed* (Catalogue and Orders) cannot be switched off. Shared state is optional: switched off, the register works on its own.\n\nThe screen opens on what the till is doing today, so looking at it changes nothing. Nothing is saved until you tap **Save choice**, and saving never moves or deletes any data. Anything already held in an older service stays there.\n\n### The connections you can choose\n- **Shopify** can supply every part except the card reader. See [[settings/shopify]].\n- **Pure Tillium** keeps the shop on this iPad, with no outside service. See [[settings/pure-tillium]].\n- **Square** supplies the catalogue, stock, customers, discounts and orders. See [[settings/square]].\n- **Zeller** is the card reader. **iCloud** shares the register's settings and totals between iPads. See [[settings/cloud-sync]].\n\n### Sign-in for a connection\nA connection that needs a login (Square, for now) shows a **sign-in** box under the rows once you have picked it. Type the details and tap **Save and check**. A secret such as an access token is never shown back: the box only says it is saved, and typing a new one replaces it. **Forget this sign-in** removes the details from this iPad and changes nothing in the service. Practice mode saves nothing. These details stay on this iPad; they are not shared with other registers.\n\n### Move my data\nFurther down is **Move my data**, which copies a shop from one connection to another. See [[settings/move-data]].\n\n### Check connections\nTap **Check connections** to ask every connection in use whether it is signed in and what it is missing. A part the login has no permission for shows a warning naming the permission to add.\n\n### Go back\nOnce a choice is saved, **Go back to the current setup** removes it, and the till reads its setup the