+   "lead": "**Move my data**, at the bottom of **More ▸ Settings ▸ Connections**, copies your shop from one connection to another. It copies, it never deletes, and it shows you what it will do first.",
+   "sections": {
+    "basic": "### Copy a shop\n1. Choose **Copy from** and **Copy to**.\n2. Tap **See what would be copied**. Nothing changes yet. You see how many items, collections and customers will be copied, what is already there, and what will be left behind.\n3. Read the warnings and the list of what is **not copied**. Tap **Copy to ...** and confirm.\n\n### What is copied\nItems with their prices, SKUs, barcodes, costs and stock; collections; and customers. Items that are archived or drafts are left behind.\n\n### What is not copied\nOrder history, gift cards (Shopify only gives the last four digits of a code), automatic discounts and presets, and pictures and sales channels. The screen lists these every time.\n\n### If it stops\nRun it again. Anything already copied is recognised and skipped, so it carries on from where it got to. After five failures in a row it stops and says why.\n\n### Practice mode\nPractice mode refuses to copy.",
+    "deep": "### How an item is matched\nBy SKU first, then barcode, then name and price. An item that matches something already in the destination is not copied again. Items with neither a SKU nor a barcode can be copied twice if you run the same copy into a destination that already holds them under a different name, so the screen warns about them.\n\n### Options\nA product with options (Size, Colour) is copied as separate items named like \"Shirt - Large\", because not every connection has options.\n\n### Customers\nMatched by email, then phone number, then name.",
+    "advanced": "| Job | Where |\n|---|---|\n| The plan: what would be copied, matched and left behind | `buildPlan` in `src/alloykit/smelter.ts` |\n| Reading each side directly (not through the router) | `readSide`, `dryRun` in `src/alloyhost/smelter.ts` |\n| The copy | `runPlan` in `src/alloyhost/smelter.ts`: items with stock, then collections, then customers |\n| The screen | `MoveData` in `src/screens/Connections.tsx` |\n\nTests: `tests/alloysmelter.test.ts`. Device test: T122 in `dev_docs/DEVICE_TESTS.md`."
