+---
+id: settings/pure-tillium
+title: Pure Tillium
+parent: settings
+summary: Run the till with no outside service: items, stock, customers, orders and gift cards are kept on this iPad.
+tags: [Pure Tillium, offline, no Shopify, local, This iPad, orders, gift cards]
+related: [settings/connections, settings/move-data, settings/backup]
+updated: 2026-11-26
+roles: [manager, owner]
+---
+Pure Tillium keeps the whole shop on this iPad. Choose it in **More ▸ Settings ▸ Connections** when you want a register that works without Shopify or Square.
+
+## Basic
+
+### What it does
+- Items, stock, collections, customers, discounts, gift cards and orders are all kept on this iPad.
+- Orders are named **#T1001**, **#T1002** and so on.
+- There is one location, **This iPad**. You do not pick a location.
+- Refunds, returns and gift cards work the way they do with Shopify. Money is shown as **Zeller**, **Cash**, **Gift card** or **Exchange credit**.
+
+### Before you switch
+Nothing is copied when you switch, and nothing is deleted. To bring your shop across, use **Move my data** ([[settings/move-data]]). Back up first ([[settings/backup]]) if the data matters.
+
+### What it cannot do yet
+- The data lives on this one iPad. Another register does not see it, and the QR setup does not copy it.
+- If this iPad is lost or reset, Pure Tillium data goes with it unless you made a backup.
+
+## Deep
+
+### Practice mode
+In practice mode Pure Tillium refuses every write, like the other connections, so practice never changes the real shop.
+
+### If it is switched off and on
+Switching away from Pure Tillium leaves its data where it is. Switching back finds it again. The location you used before is remembered and restored when you leave.
+
+## Advanced
+
+| Job | Where |
+|---|---|
+| The Alloy (every Element it supplies) | `src/alloys/tillium/alloy.ts` |
+| Storage on the iPad, one namespace per Alloy | `appLocalStore`, `scopedStore` in `src/alloyhost/persistentStore.ts` (keys `tl1:<collection>:<id>`) |
+| Writes one at a time, repeats safe on their key | the lock `L` and `once` in `src/alloys/tillium/alloy.ts` |
+| The built-in location and switching back | `LOCAL_LOCATION`, `reconcileLocation` in `src/alloyhost/choice.ts` |
+
+Tests: `tests/alloytillium.test.ts`, `tests/alloypersist.test.ts`.
+
+### Known to change
+Sharing this data between registers is not built. Until it is, treat Pure Tillium as one register.
