@@ -0,0 +1,51 @@
+---
+id: settings/square
+title: Square
+parent: settings
+summary: Use Square for items, stock, customers, discounts and orders, with a Square access token.
+tags: [Square, access token, location, sandbox, refunds, discounts, sign in]
+related: [settings/connections, settings/move-data, settings/pure-tillium]
+updated: 2026-11-26
+roles: [manager, owner]
+---
+Choose **Square** in **More ▸ Settings ▸ Connections** to keep items, stock, customers, discounts and orders on your Square account.
+
+## Basic
+
+### Set it up
+1. In the Square Developer Dashboard open your application, then Credentials, and copy the **Production** access token.
+2. In Connections choose Square for the parts you want, then paste the token in the **Square sign-in** box and tap **Save and check**.
+3. When it says Connected, tap your **location** in the list. Stock and orders are counted at that one location.
+4. Tap **Save choice**.
+
+To try it without touching your real account, type `sandbox` in the Environment box and use the Sandbox token.
+
+### What it does
+- Each sale is recorded in Square as an order, with every way it was paid.
+- Refunds are made against the payment that took the money, and returned items go back in stock unless you turn that off.
+- Fixed percentage and fixed amount discounts in Square appear as the till's discount presets.
+
+### What it does not do yet
+- Gift cards and the card reader. Use Zeller for cards.
+- Square's automatic pricing rules are not used.
+- A gift card or exchange credit cannot be refunded onto the card itself, only against its payment.
+- Each item has one price. Square item options become separate items when you copy a shop in.
+
+## Deep
+
+### If a sale will not record
+The message names the problem, such as no location chosen or the token being refused. Check the sign-in box, then **Check connections**. A sale that could not reach Square waits in the queue and is sent again with the same key, so Square never makes two orders.
+
+### Returned items
+Square does not say which items came back, so the till remembers it. The order shows how many of each line are left to return.
+
+## Advanced
+
+| Job | Where |
+|---|---|
+| The Alloy | `src/alloys/square/alloy.ts`, through `ctx.http` to Square's v2 API |
+| Order and payment per tender, rounding and tips as their own charges | `orders.record` |
+| Refunds against the order's payments | `orders.refund` (reads the order fresh, never over a payment's remaining amount) |
+| Sign-in details | [[settings/connections]], `src/alloyhost/credentials.ts` |
+
+Tests: `tests/alloysquare.test.ts` (against a fake Square). It was written from Square's documentation, so the device tests T123 and T124 are the real check.
